  "ingredients": [
    "1/2 cup pumpkin puree (unsweetened)",
    "1/2 cup ricotta cheese",
    "2 large egg",
    "1/4 cup butter (salted, melted)",
    "1/2 cup coconut flour",
    "2 teaspoon psyllium husk powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon cardamom",
    "1/2 teaspoon pumpkin pie spice",
    "1/4 cup stevia/erythritol blend (such as Swerve)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 325F. Add the wet ingredients to a bowl.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-cardamom-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-50881-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/1-Mix-Wet-Ingredients.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using an immersion blender, combine until very smooth — the ricotta can leave a gritty texture if not blended well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-cardamom-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-50881-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/2-Immersion-Blend-Wet-Ingredients.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the dry ingredients in a separate bowl, excluding the sweetener. Slowly incorporate the dry ingredients into the wet ingredients, stirring constantly.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-cardamom-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-50881-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/3-Mix-Dry-Ingredients-into-Wet-Ingredients.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the dough is beginning to form, add in the sweetener and stir to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-cardamom-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-50881-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/4-Add-Sweetener-and-Combine.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roll the dough into balls.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-cardamom-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-50881-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/5-Form-Donut-Holes-with-Hands.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20–25 minutes or until the outsides are a light golden brown and look slightly crumbly to the touch.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-cardamom-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-50881-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/6-Bake-for-20-to-25-Minutes.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the donut holes are baking, make a simple blend of extra pumpkin pie spice, sweetened to taste. Once the donut holes are out of the oven, sprinkle this over for a gorgeous presentation.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-cardamom-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-50881-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/7-Create-Erythritol-Coating.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy warm or cool. These go great with tea or coffee!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/pumpkin-cardamom-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-50881-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
